=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_7a3c (fork of p_a1b2) — Closed workspace; charger on person; evening objects at coffee table

This fork of p_a1b2 addresses the most damaging evidence against the parent: Marco's laptop was found at desk_b1 only 8 of 38 looks during 9–17 h (21 %), and his charger was found there just 1 of 38 times (3 %). The parent's "almost_always" 0–24 h blocks for those objects are simply wrong during work hours. The explanation: Marco works with his laptop closed inside a padded bag on the desk (the bag is not a tracked object, so the robot sees an empty desk), and his phone charger is clipped to his belt or in his pocket while he works (ON_PERSON). In the morning before 9 and after 17 the bag is open and the charger is back on the desk, which matches the 03:00, 09:00, 17:00, 18:00, and 23:00 sightings.

The second change is the evening-TV cluster. The remote was sighted at coffee_table_l1 at 21:00 and at floor_l_l1 / coffee_table_l1 at 22:00, never at tv_stand_l1 after 18:00. The blanket was on the couch at 21:00 but had moved to coffee_table_l1 by 22:00. So the remote and blanket migrate to the coffee table during the active TV window (≈ 20:30–22:30) and the blanket lingers there past 22:00.

The third change is Marco's water bottle. Sightings show it at desk_b1 from 08:00 to 11:00, absent from both desk and dish_rack between 11:00 and 18:00, back at dish_rack at 18:00, at sink_k1 at 19:00 (refill), and at dining_table_d1 at 20:00 (dinner). The mid-day gap is modelled as the kitchen sink area where Marco refills between work sessions.

What would refute this document: the charger sighted at desk_b1 during 10–16 h on a weekday (more than a couple of times), the remote at tv_stand_l1 during 20–22 h, or the blanket at couch_l1 at 22:00 on repeated occasions.

